        "content": "# Quick Build: Ultra-Performant JSON Validation Script\n\n**Request**: Add a JSON validation script that's ultra performant\n**Scope**: Small\n**Created**: 2026-03-07\n**Workflow**: build-fast\n**Run ID**: db96f793-c8f6-4753-8a47-e0baf7ee0abc\n\n## Context\n\n- **Stack**: Bun, TypeScript (strict mode, ESM)\n- **Patterns**: kebab-case files, camelCase functions, PascalCase types, co-located tests\n- **No external deps**: Only Bun built-ins allowed\n\n## Plan Summary\n\nCreate an ultra-performant JSON validation module using Bun/TypeScript with zero external dependencies. Focus on performance through:\n- Manual parsing validation (avoid double-parse overhead)\n- Schema-based validation with compiled validators\n- Type-safe validation results\n- Comprehensive error reporting with paths\n\n## Tasks\n\n### Task 1: Create JSON validation module\n- **ID**: task-1\n- **File**: `src/json-validator.ts`\n- **Description**: Implement a high-performance JSON validation module with:\n  - `JsonSchema` type definition supporting string, number, boolean, object, array types with nested schemas\n  - `ValidationResult` type with success flag, errors array with paths\n  - `validateJson(input: string, schema: JsonSchema): ValidationResult` — validates a JSON string against a schema\n  - `isValidJson(input: string): boolean` — fast check if string is valid JSON\n  - `parseJsonSafe<T>(input: string): { success: boolean; data?: T; error?: string }` — safe parse wrapper\n  - Performance optimizations: early exits, minimal allocations, iterative (not recursive where possible)\n\n### Task 2: Create tests for JSON validation module\n- **ID**: task-2\n- **File**: `src/json-validator.test.ts`\n- **Description**: Comprehensive tests using Bun's test runner:\n  - Test `isValidJson` with valid/invalid inputs\n  - Test `parseJsonSafe` with valid JSON, invalid JSON, edge cases\n  - Test `validateJson` with various schema types (string, number, boolean, object, array)\n  - Test nested object validation\n  - Test required fields validation\n  - Test array item validation\n  - Test error path reporting\n  - Test performance (validate large JSON quickly)\n\n### Task 3: Add validate script to package.json\n- **ID**: task-3\n- **File**: `package.json`\n- **Description**: Add a `\"validate\"` script entry: `\"validate\": \"bun run src/json-validator.ts\"` so the validator can be run standalone\n\n## Files Affected\n\n- `src/json-validator.ts` (new)\n- `src/json-validator.test.ts` (new)\n- `package.json` (modified — add script)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. All validation functions are exported and typed\n2. Zero external dependencies\n3. All tests pass via `bun test`\n4. Existing tests still pass\n5. Handles edge cases: empty strings, deeply nested objects, large arrays\n6. Returns structured error information with JSON paths\n"
